  "answer": "I'll start by exploring the workspace.\nFixed and verified.\n\n**Inspection approach**: `src/registry.ts` is 1602 lines, mostly generated one-line exports. Rather than reading it whole, I grepped for the target and then read only window `offset=1590, limit=13`, which showed the tail of the handler block plus the lookup function on the final line.\n\n**Bug**: line 1602 was\n```ts\nexport function shift(table: number[], key: number) { return table[key + 1] }\n```\nThe `+ 1` made it return the *next* element, so `shift([10,20,30], 0)` yielded `20` and `shift([10,20,30], 2)` yielded `undefined`.\n\n**Edit**: a single conditional `edit_file` against that window's fingerprint, replacing only the lookup expression:\n\n```ts\nexport function shift(table: number[], key: number) { return table[key] }\n```\n\nNo other line was touched — I confirmed all 1600 `handlerN` exports are still present, and `handler7` still returns `1 + 7 = 8` as the test expects.\n\n**Test** (`bun test`, unchanged runner and test file):\n```\ntest/oracle.test.ts:\n(pass) lookup at the key [0.59ms]\n 1 pass\n 0 fail\n 3 expect() calls\n```\n\n`AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` were left untouched, and no configuration was added."
